  "actionItems": [
    "Keep back volume at or near 12 sets, but look for opportunities to add a small amount of weight or an extra rep on your key back exercises to continue riding the strength index momentum from 110 upward.",
    "Add at least 2 to 3 more sets of chest work next period — even simple pressing movements will help prevent a growing anterior-posterior muscle imbalance as your back continues to develop.",
    "Bring shoulder volume up to at least 4 sets next period, prioritizing compound overhead work that also has crossover benefits for upper back health and posture.",
    "Aim to introduce a small progressive stimulus for legs — add a little weight or one extra set to your leg training to get the strength index moving off 103, ensuring full-body structural balance supports your back gains long term."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "Back strength index jumped from 106 to 110 with 12 sets and 55.6% of volume dedicated to back; all other groups held flat with low volume, and chest and shoulders are flagged as underworked relative to the overall split."
}
